  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, $\\cos \\theta+\\sin \\theta+\\frac{2}{\\sin 2 \\theta}, \\theta \\in\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$\r\nFor minimum value, $\\sin 2 \\theta$ must be maximum\r\n$\\therefore \\quad 2 \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\nHence, $\\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{2}{\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2}}=\\sqrt{2}+2$",
